digraph decision_tree {
  rankdir=TB;
  bgcolor="#0d0e12";
  node [shape=box, style="rounded,filled", fontname="Helvetica", fontsize=10, fillcolor="#181a20", color="#343846", fontcolor="#e2e8f0"];
  edge [color="#64748b", fontcolor="#94a3b8", fontsize=9, fontname="Helvetica"];

  history [
    label="1. Prior-journal learning pass (python3 scripts/stats.py, 2026-11-04T14:32Z)\n18 folders: 2 WIN, 5 LOSS, 4 EXPIRED+/-%, 4 EXPIRED (never filled), 1 PENDING (XRP). Sum +3.69%, WR 28.6%.\nLessons used here, each checked against that folder's review.md / trade.toml / decision_tree.dot:\n- LOSS-0.72%_2026-10-29T1149Z_BTCUSDT (same symbol, same setup shape): short at the 80300 cap with the stop\n  580 pts above it, swept 6h later by a squeeze, then price fell 4 days later. Lesson carried: at BTC a cap\n  that has been tested repeatedly can break upward first; a stop inside ~1x 1h ATR above the cap does not survive.\n  Applied today by NOT fading the cap that had just broken (that candidate was never built).\n- LOSS-1.30%_2026-10-19T1533Z_XRPUSDT: same error - fading a level as momentum went through it, stop inside the\n  reach of the squeeze. Reinforces the same rule.\n- WIN+1.26%_2026-10-27T0919Z_ASTERUSDT: the one winner was a fade whose stop sat 0.2-0.4% BEYOND the measured\n  extreme rather than inside the noise band. Applied: SL 78050 sits below the tested 78001.77 low and the 78000\n  round number, not above them.\n- EXPIRED_2026-11-02T0954Z_SOLUSDT + EXPIRED_2026-10-25T1228Z_CAKEUSDT + EXPIRED_2026-11-01T1010Z_ASTERUSDT\n  (all settled this run): three of four recent no-fills were limits parked at a range extreme the market never\n  revisited. Applied: entry 78900 is only 0.56% below the live price, on a level Jev prices at P(fill) 0.66,\n  rather than at a far edge.\n- EXPIRED+1.14%_ZECUSDT / EXPIRED+1.73%_UNIUSDT / EXPIRED+3.95%_ASTERUSDT: non-TP exits are often partial\n  gains, so the neither-branch is carried explicitly rather than assumed to be zero-or-loss.\nn=11 settled, single outlier (ASTER +3.95% expiry) - no directional inference taken from aggregates.",
    fillcolor="#1e293b", color="#3b82f6"
  ];

  extract [
    label="2. Chart extraction (image 261104_15h31m25s_screenshot.png, BTCUSDT 1h Aster, footer clock\n15:31:25 UTC+1 = 2026-11-04T14:31Z; header O78340.3 H78596.7 L78176.1 C78567.2)\n253 hourly candles 2026-10-25T02:00Z..2026-11-04T14:00Z pixel-read (price = 82500 - 7.8342*(y-65),\n5.954 px/h, last bar = 14:00Z). Validation: axis label centres y=384 -> 80001, y=256 -> 81003; the\nreplica reproduces the header of the final bar within 0.01%. The 07:00Z..14:00Z closes and the 14:00Z\nhigh/low were then replaced with real Binance spot values (server time 14:45:57Z, last 79349.04,\n24h H 79558.79 L 75736.38).\nMeasured structure: 29 Oct 16:00Z high 81936 (breakdown origin) -> 30 Oct 02:00Z low 76476 (-6.7% in 10h).\nFive-day base: flat top 78690-78841 with FOUR touches (78771 on 30 Oct, 78841 on 2 Nov, 78693 and 78700\non 4 Nov); descending lows 76476 -> 76280 -> 76687 -> 76382 -> 75700 (4 Nov 03:00Z, reclaimed same hour,\nclose 76468). 4 Nov rally +3.8% off 75700 into the base top. Also measured: 79750-80000 prior congestion\nshelf, 80100-80350 last congestion before the 29 Oct break, 80494 (29 Oct 05:00 high). Est 1h ATR 850-900\npts (1.1%); 24h range 3.5%.",
    fillcolor="#0f2a43", color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  reanchor [
    label="3. RE-ANCHOR at 2026-11-04T14:50Z (live Binance spot 79349.04, 14:00Z bar H 79558.79 L 78210 C 79326.78)\n+1.0% above the capture price. The five-day base top 78690-78841 broke to the upside inside that hour.\nJev (noul): 'the 14:35Z fade setup is still valid at the live price' p=0.12 (unlikely, auto) -> the setup\ncontemplated from the image is VOID and is not carried forward as a candidate. Both directions re-evaluated\nfrom the live price; the chart replay stays in graphpoints.csv and chart.svg, the decision does not.",
    fillcolor="#3b1d1d", color="#ef4444"
  ];

  scenarios [
    label="4. Scenarios (Jev noul at the live price, overlapping yes/no, window 2026-11-04T15:00Z..2026-11-06T08:00Z)\n- >=79850 before <=78841 p=0.39 ; <=78841 before >=79850 p=0.70 (pullback first is the modal path)\n- <=78500 at all by Fri 08:00Z p=0.70 ; <=78900 at all by Thu 20:00Z p=0.71\n- impulse holds above 78841 for most of the next 24h p=0.55 (breakout only marginally favoured to hold)\n- close above 78900 at 2026-11-06T06:00Z p=0.47\n- max pain 79,000 pulls price toward 79,000 rather than 80,000+ p=0.67\n- the breakout makes the long side the better risk-adjusted opportunity p=0.46 (direction is close to a coin flip)\nRead: a retest-then-bounce path inside 78000-80000 into a 79,000-pin expiry. Not a directional bet; the\nticket is an entry-location bet on the retest of a level that just flipped from resistance to support.\nNo scenario probability was summed or normalised anywhere in the arithmetic.",
    fillcolor="#1e1b4b", color="#8b5cf6"
  ];

  research [
    label="5. Research (Jev-defined agenda: jev_decide events 0.64 vs liq_map 0.18, catalyst 0.15, flows 0.01,\nskip_research 0.01; all three requirements supported for 'events'). One agent pass, snapshots 14:40-14:50Z,\nfull log in research_log.txt. Material dated findings:\n- Deribit weekly BTC options expiry Fri 2026-11-06T08:00Z, ~$2.5-3.6B, max pain 79,000, P/C 0.34-0.47,\n  call walls 82,000/85,000, put clusters 74,000/75,000 -> pinning risk, not a directional impulse.\n- US NFP Fri 2026-11-06T13:30Z (cons 45-60K, prior 29K) -> the only genuine impulse risk in the window.\n- No FOMC, CPI, CME expiry, BTC unlock or regulatory date inside the window.\n- Background: Democrat midterm sweep 3 Nov, DXY five-week low, gold +2.8%; Binance $6.3B hack 29 Oct still\n  an overhang; ETF outflows 5 straight sessions, average cost basis ~81,500; funding 0.01%/8h; OI -0.3%.\n- Could not be found: the ISM Services actual (pages still pending at 14:44Z); the cause of the 14:00Z\n  impulse is therefore NOT attributed to a print in this log - midterm risk-on is labelled inference.\nAgenda effect: the research did not move the direction (Jev still 0.46 on 'long is the better side'), it\nmoved the EXPIRY to 06:00Z on 6 Nov, two hours before the 79,000-pin expiry and 7.5h before NFP, so that\nneither event decides the ticket.",
    fillcolor="#14261c", color="#22c55e"
  ];

  jev [
    label="6. Jev propositions recorded verbatim (probability)\n(a) original fade still valid at live price 0.12 (unlikely, auto)\n(b) buy limit 78900 filled before 2026-11-06T06:00Z 0.66\n(c) cond on a 78900 fill: touches 79850 before 78050 0.63 / 78050 before 79850 0.27 / neither 0.15\n(d) cond on a 78900 fill: touches 80000 before 78050 0.37\n(e) close above 78900 at 2026-11-06T06:00Z 0.47\n(f) sell limit 79850 filled before 2026-11-06T06:00Z 0.45; cond 78900 before 80400 0.69 / 80400 first 0.22\n(g) cond on buying at 79349: 80350 before 78550 within 40h 0.38\n(h) cond on selling at 79349: 78500 before 79650 within 40h 0.45\n(i) buying the retest at 78900 beats buying now 0.64\n(j) breakout holds above 78841 most of 24h 0.55 ; long side is the better opportunity 0.46\n(k) max pain pulls to 79,000 rather than 80,000+ 0.67\nFinal battery (jev_decide): long_retest_78900 0.71, short_shelf_79850 0.15, no_trade 0.07,\nshort_market_now 0.01, none 0.06, ask_user 0, investigate 0. Winner: all 3 requirements supported,\nnone contradicted. short_shelf_79850 contradicted on 'stop outside the noise band'; short_market_now\ncontradicted on BOTH 'entry justified by structure' and 'stop outside the noise band'; no_trade\ncontradicted on 'expected net outcome positive'.",
    fillcolor="#272015", color="#eab308"
  ];

  candidates [
    label="7. Candidates (LONG and SHORT evaluated independently; journal model: no fees/funding/slippage,\nLIMIT fills on touch, TP ignored in the fill candle, both-touched = LOSS, unfilled = EXPIRED with 0 payoff)\nA) LONG LIMIT 78900 / TP 79850 / SL 78050 / expire 2026-11-06T06:00Z   <= SELECTED\n   P(fill) 0.66 | cond TP-first 0.63 | cond SL-first 0.27 | neither 0.15 (P(close>78900 at expiry) 0.47)\n   G +1.20406% L -1.07731% RR 1.118 p_BE 0.4722 | EV/fill +0.46768% | EV/order +0.30867%\nB) A with TP 80000: G +1.39417% RR 1.294 p_BE 0.4359, but cond TP-first only 0.37 -> EV/order +0.09871%,\nmargin over p_BE NEGATIVE (-0.0659). REJECTED - the extra 0.19% of target costs the trade its edge.\nC) SHORT LIMIT 79850 / TP 78900 / SL 80400: P(fill) 0.45, cond TP-first 0.69, G +1.18973% L -0.68879%\nRR 1.727 p_BE 0.3667, EV/order +0.30122% - economically equivalent to A, but its fill needs the >=79850\n-first sequence Jev rates 0.39, and its stop sits inside the 79750-80400 congestion band (jev_decide:\n'stop outside the noise band' contradicted). REJECTED.\nD) LONG MARKET 79349 / TP 80350 / SL 78550: cond TP-first 0.38 vs p_BE 0.4439 -> EV -0.14493%/trade.\nNEGATIVE. REJECTED (and it chases a 1.7% impulse bar).\nE) SHORT MARKET 79349 / TP 78500 / SL 79650: EV +0.27285%, but the 0.38% stop is 0.35x ATR and already\ninside the printed range of the live 14:00Z bar; fading a level as it breaks is exactly LOSS-0.72%/BTCUSDT\nand LOSS-1.30%/XRPUSDT. jev_decide contradicted it on two of three requirements. REJECTED.\nF) A with a tighter stop 78250 (RR 1.46): cond TP-first falls to 0.56 while cond SL-first rises to 0.43\n-> EV/order +0.20482%. REJECTED: 78250 sits just above the 78210 low of the impulse bar, i.e. inside noise,\nand the wider stop dominates on EV.\nG) NO_TRADE: rebutted - option A is positive under every tested probability and jev_decide contradicted\nno_trade's 'expected net outcome positive' requirement.",
    fillcolor="#1f242d", color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  math [
    label="8. Selected-ticket arithmetic (script, exact)\nentry 78900 (0.56% below the live 79349; the 78690-78841 base top that broke at 14:00Z is the fill zone)\nTP 79850 (just under the 79750-80000 pre-breakdown congestion shelf; below the 80000 level whose reclaim\n  failed on 29 Oct, so the target does not require the breakout to be a new trend)\nSL 78050 (below the tested 78001.77 low of 4 Nov 12:00Z and the 78000 round number; ~0.98x est 1h ATR)\nG = (79850-78900)/78900 = +1.20406%   L = (78900-78050)/78900 = -1.07731%   RR 1.118\np_BE = L/(G+L) = 0.4722   vs   P(TP first | fill) = 0.63   -> margin +0.1578\nEV/fill  = 0.63*1.20406 - 0.27*1.07731 = +0.46768%   (neither-branch credited 0; upper bound +0.558%/fill)\nEV/order = P(fill)*EV/fill = 0.66*0.46768 = +0.30867% ; P(no fill) 0.34 pays 0 (EXPIRED)\nSensitivity: TP-first 0.70/0.55/0.50/0.472 -> EV/order +0.414/-+0.210/+0.141/+0.091%\n             P(fill) 0.75/0.55/0.45 -> EV/order +0.351/+0.257/+0.210%\nPositive for every tested combination; break-even TP-first is 0.4722 and was never assumed as achieved.\nFees/funding/slippage do not exist in this model and were not invented; a 0.05-0.10% round trip would lift\np_BE to ~0.513-0.552, which 0.63 still clears (EV/order would fall to ~+0.18%).",
    fillcolor="#1f242d", color="#38bdf8"
  ];

  forecast [
    label="9. Independent forecast (built before the ticket was finalised; contested; graphpoints.csv 15:00Z..06:00Z,\nchart_prediction.svg)\nModal path: 15:00Z 79340 -> staircase down through the old cap to 78900 by 19:00Z (the fill), dip to\n78500 at 23:00Z (the level Jev rates 0.70 likely to be touched), then a higher grind 78790 -> 79240 ->\n79540 -> peak 79860 at Thu 20:00Z (TP zone), easing back to 79100 at the 06:00Z Friday expiry.\nSo the forecast reaches entry first, then TP on Thursday evening, then drifts to just above entry at expiry.\nDissent carried: the 0.39 'straight up through 79850 first' branch would leave the order unfilled\n(pays 0); the 0.27 immediate-slide branch through 78050 would stop it (capped at -1.08%). The path was not\nbent to make the ticket qualify - it is the retest-then-bounce shape Jev's own probabilities describe.",
    fillcolor="#2a2338", color="#c084fc"
  ];

  checks [
    label="10. Contradictions and robustness\n- Chart vs live price: the chart-fade setup was invalidated (0.12). Handled by re-anchoring, not by keeping\nthe stale levels; the IDEA folder records both states.\n- Overlap sanity: TP-first 0.63 + SL-first 0.27 + neither 0.15 = 1.05 (separate yes/no wordings, overlapping).\nNot normalised, not summed, not used as a distribution anywhere.\n- Direction is close to a coin flip (0.46 'long is the better side') and the ticket does not depend on it:\nits edge comes from the entry location (jev 0.64 'retest beats buying now') and from the stop sitting\noutside noise. Recorded rather than hidden.\n- Mid-point fill logic: entry 78900 is BELOW every recent print (live 79349, 14:00Z low 78210 came from a\nsweep that already happened). The order therefore only fills if price returns, and the fill candle is the one\nstraddling place_at, which the resolver skips - no instantaneous artificial fill.\n- Timing: expiry 2026-11-06T06:00Z stops 2h before the Deribit 08:00Z weekly expiry (max pain 79,000) and\n7.5h before NFP 13:30Z, so neither scheduled event can decide the result.\n- Research limit: the 14:00Z impulse's cause was not identified; if it is a one-hour spike rather than a\nreal flow shift, the 0.27 SL-first branch is understated. That risk is priced by the 78050 stop, not ignored.\n- n=11 settled trades in the journal with one outlier: no aggregate win-rate inference used to pick the side.",
    fillcolor="#2d1b24", color="#f43f5e"
  ];

  terminal [
    label="FINAL DECISION: GO_LIMIT (PENDING)\nBTCUSDT LONG LIMIT 78900 | TP 79850 (+1.20406%) | SL 78050 (-1.07731%) | RR 1.12\nP(fill) 0.66 | P(TP before SL | fill) 0.63 | p_BE 0.4722 | EV/fill +0.46768% | EV/order +0.30867%\nExpire 2026-11-06T06:00:00Z (2h before the Deribit weekly expiry at 08:00Z, 7.5h before NFP)\nFolder: IDEA_2026-11-04T1432Z_BTCUSDT",
    shape=ellipse, fillcolor="#1e293b", color="#eab308", fontcolor="#fef08a"
  ];

  history -> extract; extract -> reanchor; reanchor -> scenarios; scenarios -> research; research -> jev;
  jev -> candidates; candidates -> math; scenarios -> forecast; math -> checks; forecast -> checks;
  candidates -> checks [style=dashed, color="#ef4444", label="rejected B,C,D,E,F,G"];
  checks -> terminal;
}